{"uid":"2bc0fe7a3aafb57d","name":"test_the_quantifier_rewrite_keeps_the_clauses_own_demand[each-shipped-piece]","fullName":"tests.test_legal_rewrite_reprompt#test_the_quantifier_rewrite_keeps_the_clauses_own_demand","historyId":"07674e38fbfe207421035745a25a3f43","time":{"start":1792160656724,"stop":1792160656727,"duration":3},"description":"The clause's own words -- subject, verb and the demand it makes --\n    survive into the rewrite verbatim; the rewrite only ADDS the bound the\n    lint is missing, as a CONCRETE, already-runnable observable\n    (`pytest`) -- never a backticked fill-in slot that only tells the\n    planner to go name a bound itself (cure-01-01, PRD requirement B.1,\n    #135: the first cure of this exact gap emitted precisely that\n    fill-in slot -- `` `<the one file or command that lists the widget\n    set>` `` -- in the actual next planner prompt, and this test asserted\n    it verbatim).\n\n    The \"every-widget-works\" case additionally folds in this task's OWN\n    named regressions (no new collected test item is added -- the fast\n    tier's collected count is pinned, `tests/test_tier_budgets.py`) for\n    both \"Every widget works.\" and \"Each handler returns a value.\": each\n    proves that the offered rewrite preserves the offending clause's own\n    demand, is a concrete bounded observable with no unresolved\n    placeholder, and is itself accepted by the unchanged applicable lints.\n\n    #209 defect 1: that second half used to drive two real loop runs and\n    assert the rewrite arrived in `iterations/0002/prompt.md` beside \"Your\n    previous plan-proposal.json was rejected\" -- the refusal itself. The\n    rewrite is now APPLIED in a pre-pass instead of quoted as advice, so\n    there is no rejected-proposal re-ask to carry it: the loop-level half\n    asserts the bounded criteria reached `tasks.json` on the FIRST planning\n    iteration, that no planning `contract.violation` was recorded at all,\n    and that iteration 0002 is the worker's. Every direct-rewrite\n    assertion in the first half, and every one in this loop over the two\n    named regressions, is kept verbatim -- what the rewrite says is\n    unchanged; only where it is delivered changed.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The clause's own words -- subject, verb and the demand it makes --<br />\nsurvive into the rewrite verbatim; the rewrite only ADDS the bound the<br />\nlint is missing, as a CONCRETE, already-runnable observable<br />\n(<code>pytest</code>) -- never a backticked fill-in slot that only tells the<br />\nplanner to go name a bound itself (cure-01-01, PRD requirement B.1,<br />\n#135: the first cure of this exact gap emitted precisely that<br />\nfill-in slot -- <code>`&lt;the one file or command that lists the widget set&gt;`</code> -- in the actual next planner prompt, and this test asserted<br />\nit verbatim).</p>\n<pre><code>The &quot;every-widget-works&quot; case additionally folds in this task's OWN\nnamed regressions (no new collected test item is added -- the fast\ntier's collected count is pinned, `tests/test_tier_budgets.py`) for\nboth &quot;Every widget works.&quot; and &quot;Each handler returns a value.&quot;: each\nproves that the offered rewrite preserves the offending clause's own\ndemand, is a concrete bounded observable with no unresolved\nplaceholder, and is itself accepted by the unchanged applicable lints.\n\n#209 defect 1: that second half used to drive two real loop runs and\nassert the rewrite arrived in `iterations/0002/prompt.md` beside &quot;Your\nprevious plan-proposal.json was rejected&quot; -- the refusal itself. The\nrewrite is now APPLIED in a pre-pass instead of quoted as advice, so\nthere is no rejected-proposal re-ask to carry it: the loop-level half\nasserts the bounded criteria reached `tasks.json` on the FIRST planning\niteration, that no planning `contract.violation` was recorded at all,\nand that iteration 0002 is the worker's. Every direct-rewrite\nassertion in the first half, and every one in this loop over the two\nnamed regressions, is kept verbatim -- what the rewrite says is\nunchanged; only where it is delivered changed.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792160405917,"stop":1792160405917,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792160405917,"stop":1792160405917,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1792160656683,"stop":1792160656684,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1792160656684,"stop":1792160656696,"duration":12},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1792160656697,"stop":1792160656697,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1792160656697,"stop":1792160656710,"duration":13},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_escalation_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start"